# multiplai-kit — PROFILE OVERRIDE TEMPLATE
# Copy to env.<name> (e.g., env.work, env.personal):  cp env.example env.work
# Use with: ./claude.sh --profile <name>
#
# A profile is an overlay sourced AFTER .env, so it overrides the fields it
# names and leaves the rest (workspace, API keys, container settings) to .env.
# Git identity is what it's for, but any variable is allowed — including
# GCP_KEY_FILE, when a client's service-account key should follow their profile
# rather than apply to every launch. Values here are forwarded to the container
# under the same rules as .env (non-empty only), and your shell still wins over
# both.
#
# NOT TO BE CONFUSED WITH .env.example (with a dot), which is the template for
# the base config file .env. See README.md → "Environment Configuration".

GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Your Name"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="you@company.com"
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Your Name"
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="you@company.com"

# macOS Keychain key for GitHub token (different per org). This is the general
# *_KEYCHAIN convention: FOO_KEYCHAIN=<item> exports <item>'s value as FOO, so
# any per-identity secret can live in the Keychain rather than in this file —
# e.g. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_KEYCHAIN="anthropic-key-myorg". See .env.example.
GH_TOKEN_KEYCHAIN="gh-token-myorg"

# --- or --- a GitHub App for this identity, instead of a PAT. Names a host-side
# App profile (~/.local/state/multiplai-gh-token/<app>/); each launch mints a
# fresh ~1-hour installation token and the App key never leaves the Mac.
# A profile may pick a different App per identity — that is the point of putting
# it here. Setup: container/docs/gh-app-token.md.
#
# EXCLUSIVE with the two lines above: declaring GH_TOKEN_APP in the same file (or
# in .env) as GH_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN_KEYCHAIN is a hard launch error. One identity
# per profile.
# GH_TOKEN_APP="myorg-app"

# Claude credentials file — separate per profile for different Claude accounts.
# Each profile gets its own OAuth credentials, so you can use a personal
# subscription for personal work and a Teams/Enterprise account for work.
# Use an absolute path; $HOME is OK (expanded at source time), but not ~.
# CLAUDE_CREDENTIALS_FILE="$HOME/.claude-container/credentials-myorg.json"

# Gemini CLI credentials directory — separate per profile for different Google accounts.
# Use an absolute path; $HOME is OK (expanded at source time), but not ~.
# GEMINI_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.gemini-work"

# GCP service-account key for this identity — mounted read-only in the container
# at /home/agent/.gcp/key.json. Set-but-missing is a hard error, so only name a
# path that exists on this machine.
# GCP_KEY_FILE="$HOME/.gcp/client-service-account.json"
# CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT="client-gcp-project"

# --- pi coding agent (./pi.sh) ---------------------------------------------
# Any variable named here is forwarded into the container when non-empty, so a
# provider key for a pi profile just goes in this file. The deepseek profile
# expects DEEPSEEK_API_KEY; other profiles declare their own in
# dotfiles/pi-profiles/<name>/required-env.txt. `/login` inside pi works too and
# stores the key in the profile instead. See docs/pi.md.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-..."
